module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.EtaleLocalRingNoetherian
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.GeometricStalkBaseChange
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Length.HenselizationBaseChange

/-!
# Length is unchanged by the base change from an étale chart to a geometric point

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S`, let `x̄` be a geometric point of `X` and let
`φ : (U, ū) → (X, x̄)` be a small étale neighbourhood whose chart `U` is a scheme, with `u` the
image in `U` of the chosen lift of `x̄`. The canonical map
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing` identifies `𝒪_{X, x̄}` with a strict
henselization of `𝒪_{U, u}` (Stacks 04KF), so it is flat and local and carries the maximal ideal
of `𝒪_{U, u}` onto the maximal ideal of `𝒪_{X, x̄}`.

Consequently the base change `- ⊗_{𝒪_{U, u}} 𝒪_{X, x̄}` of Stacks 05VP preserves the length of
every module: the fibre `𝒪_{X, x̄} / 𝔪_u 𝒪_{X, x̄}` is the residue field of `𝒪_{X, x̄}`, so the
length identity of Stacks 02M1 collapses to an equality.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.map_maximalIdeal_chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing`: the maximal ideal
  of `𝒪_{X, x̄}` is generated by the image of the maximal ideal of `𝒪_{U, u}`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocalHom_chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing`: the canonical map is a
  local homomorphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.length_chartStalkBaseChange_obj`: the base-change functor
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartStalkBaseChange` preserves lengths.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.length_chartStalkTensorEtaleLocalRing`: the left-hand side of
  Stacks 05VP has, over `𝒪_{X, x̄}`, the length that the Zariski stalk `(φ^* F)_u` has over
  `𝒪_{U, u}`.

## Implementation notes

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocalRing_etaleLocalRing` (Stacks 08AH) is a theorem and not an
instance in this development, so the two statements that mention the maximal ideal of
`𝒪_{X, x̄}` carry it as a `letI` in their own statement, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCohenMacaulayLocalRing_etaleLocalRing` does.  The two length
statements do not need it at all: `Module.length` asks only for a module.

Locality of the canonical map is deduced from the statement about maximal ideals through
`IsLocalRing.local_hom_TFAE`, rather than by composing locality of the structure map of the
henselization with locality of the comparison of Stacks 04KF; the two routes give the same
proposition and the first needs no `Nontrivial` side condition.

**No declaration here carries `@[stacks 0EE1]`.** Tag 0EE1 states that the length of a
quasi-coherent module `F` at a geometric point `x̄`, namely `length_{𝒪_{X, x̄}} F_{x̄}`, agrees
with `length_{𝒪_{U, u}} (F|_U)_u` on some, equivalently every, étale scheme chart through the
underlying point of `x̄`.  Its proof has two halves.  The half proved here is the
ring-theoretic one: lengths are unchanged by the base change along `𝒪_{U, u} → 𝒪_{X, x̄}`.
The other half is Stacks 05VP, the identification
`F_{x̄} = (F|_U)_u ⊗_{𝒪_{U, u}} 𝒪_{X, x̄}` — that is, that
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartStalkTensorEtaleLocalRing` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.geometricModuleStalk` are isomorphic — and that is absent from this
development; see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/GeometricStalkBaseChange.lean`, which record that its
proof needs Stacks 03LZ, and those of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ChartModuleRestriction.lean` and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/QuasicoherentEtaleChart.lean`, which record the
quasi-coherence gap Stacks 03LZ rests on in turn.  Given that isomorphism, Tag 0EE1 follows
from `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.length_chartStalkTensorEtaleLocalRing` together with the
existence of a small étale neighbourhood of a geometric point
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.nonempty_smallEtaleNeighborhood`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02M1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02M1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04KF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04KF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05VP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08AH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08AH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EE1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EE1)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory IsLocalRing Opposite TopologicalSpace

universe u m

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  (X : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) (hX : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS X)

/-- The maximal ideal of `𝒪_{X, x̄}` is generated by the image of the maximal ideal of
`𝒪_{U, u}` under the canonical map of Stacks 05VP.

The canonical map factors as the structure map of `𝒪_{U, u}` into the strict henselization in
its henselization tower, for which this is
`IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.map_maximalIdeal`, followed by the comparison of Stacks 04KF,
which is a ring isomorphism. -/
theorem map_maximalIdeal_chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing {x : GeometricPoint B S hS X}
    (V : SmallEtaleNeighborhood x) :
    letI : IsLocalRing ↥(etaleLocalRing B S hS X x) := isLocalRing_etaleLocalRing B S hS X hX x
    Ideal.map (chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing B S hS X hX V)
        (maximalIdeal ↥(chartLocalRing B S hS X V)) =
      maximalIdeal ↥(etaleLocalRing B S hS X x) := by
  have : IsLocalRing ↥(etaleLocalRing B S hS X x) := isLocalRing_etaleLocalRing B S hS X hX x
  have hsh : Ideal.map (algebraMap ↥(chartLocalRing B S hS X V)
        (chartHenselizationTower B S hS X V).strictHenselization)
        (maximalIdeal ↥(chartLocalRing B S hS X V)) =
      maximalIdeal (chartHenselizationTower B S hS X V).strictHenselization :=
    IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.map_maximalIdeal
      (L := separableClosure (ResidueField ↥(chartLocalRing B S hS X V))
        (chartGeometricPoint V).residueField)
  rw [chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing, ← Ideal.map_map, hsh,
    map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective _ (chartStrictHenselizationEquiv B S hS X hX V).surjective]

/-- The canonical map `𝒪_{U, u} → 𝒪_{X, x̄}` of Stacks 05VP is a local homomorphism. -/
theorem isLocalHom_chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing {x : GeometricPoint B S hS X}
    (V : SmallEtaleNeighborhood x) :
    letI : IsLocalRing ↥(etaleLocalRing B S hS X x) := isLocalRing_etaleLocalRing B S hS X hX x
    IsLocalHom (chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing B S hS X hX V) := by
  have : IsLocalRing ↥(etaleLocalRing B S hS X x) := isLocalRing_etaleLocalRing B S hS X hX x
  exact ((local_hom_TFAE (chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing B S hS X hX V)).out 3 1).mp
    (map_maximalIdeal_chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing B S hS X hX V).le

/-- **The base change of Stacks 05VP preserves lengths.** For every module `N` over the local
ring `𝒪_{U, u}` of an étale scheme chart, the base change `N ⊗_{𝒪_{U, u}} 𝒪_{X, x̄}` has the
same length over `𝒪_{X, x̄}` as `N` has over `𝒪_{U, u}`.

The canonical map is flat
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing`) and local, and the maximal
ideal of `𝒪_{X, x̄}` is extended from `𝒪_{U, u}`, so this is
`length_baseChange_eq_of_map_maximalIdeal`. -/
theorem length_chartStalkBaseChange_obj {x : GeometricPoint B S hS X}
    (V : SmallEtaleNeighborhood x) (N : ModuleCat.{max u m} ↥(chartLocalRing B S hS X V)) :
    Module.length ↥(etaleLocalRing B S hS X x)
        ((chartStalkBaseChange.{u, m} B S hS X hX V).obj N) =
      Module.length ↥(chartLocalRing B S hS X V) N := by
  have : IsLocalRing ↥(etaleLocalRing B S hS X x) := isLocalRing_etaleLocalRing B S hS X hX x
  let _ : Algebra ↥(chartLocalRing B S hS X V) ↥(etaleLocalRing B S hS X x) :=
    (chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing B S hS X hX V).toAlgebra
  have _ : Module.Flat ↥(chartLocalRing B S hS X V) ↥(etaleLocalRing B S hS X x) :=
    flat_chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing B S hS X hX V
  have _ : IsLocalHom (algebraMap ↥(chartLocalRing B S hS X V)
      ↥(etaleLocalRing B S hS X x)) :=
    isLocalHom_chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing B S hS X hX V
  exact (length_baseChange_eq_of_map_maximalIdeal _ _
    (map_maximalIdeal_chartLocalRingToEtaleLocalRing B S hS X hX V) N).symm

/-- **The left-hand side of Stacks 05VP has the length of the Zariski stalk.** For an
`𝒪_X`-module `F` and a small étale neighbourhood `(U, ū)` of a geometric point `x̄` with `U` a
scheme, the module `(φ^* F)_u ⊗_{𝒪_{U, u}} 𝒪_{X, x̄}` has, over `𝒪_{X, x̄}`, the length that the
ordinary (Zariski) stalk `(φ^* F)_u` has over `𝒪_{U, u}`.

Stacks 05VP asserts that the left-hand side is the geometric stalk `F_{x̄}`; with that
identification this is the comparison of lengths which Stacks 0EE1 is about. See the
implementation notes of this file. -/
theorem length_chartStalkTensorEtaleLocalRing {x : GeometricPoint B S hS X}
    (V : SmallEtaleNeighborhood x) (F : Modules.{u, m} B S hS X hX) :
    Module.length ↥(etaleLocalRing B S hS X x)
        (chartStalkTensorEtaleLocalRing.{u, m} B S hS X hX V F) =
      Module.length ↥(chartLocalRing B S hS X V) (chartZariskiModuleStalk B S hS X hX V F) :=
  length_chartStalkBaseChange_obj B S hS X hX V _

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
